(\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{3}}{\\cancel{3}\\cdot \\cancel{2}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{6}{1}) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "104d699a-65f0-5f9c-99d0-9f74f993a68b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442338} {:answer/id #uuid "1fed7d6c-2be1-5cec-bd7e-8f752ef6b918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442347} {:answer/id #uuid "3386c3ad-9434-5e15-919e-f742474174c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442351} {:answer/id #uuid "46c2713e-c655-5a9d-ab4d-07367762c4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442357} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e3ba24-3a51-51d3-b8a4-81746a3ba719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "104d699a-65f0-5f9c-99d0-9f74f993a68b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442338} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0e026c-829d-5bf5-9811-b53905fa0394" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "319279a3-ba94-5bbe-b88b-0e4da5c9c0b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-99503" :question/problem "$4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{16})=$" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of a positive number and a negative number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{16})=-(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{16})\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{16}) & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{16}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{4\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 3}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
